      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get both of those points but it feels like they're totally different things. one is about biology/physics and the other is about social rights. if we're talking about competitive advantage and fairness in performance, doesnt the biological argument just outweigh the social one? like, isnt it objectively more important to have a level playing field based on physical reality?",
